#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""kiwi-killswitchd — fail-closed VPN kill switch / firewall manager (root daemon).

One stateful process that:
  * owns the nftables kill switch (`inet kiwi_ks` + optional `netdev kiwi_ks_egress`)
  * watches NetworkManager AND the kernel and re-syncs on every relevant change
  * steers systemd-resolved so DNS cannot leak around the tunnel
  * exposes a D-Bus system interface (eu.kiwinetwork.KillSwitch), passwordless for
    the `wheel` group via the bus policy — no pkexec, no polkit prompt

It protects exactly ONE VPN connection at a time. It never starts or stops a VPN:
the user owns their connections, the daemon observes them and builds the firewall.

Only PyGObject (GLib/Gio) + the stdlib are used, plus nft/ip/nmcli/wg/resolvectl —
everything is in the Silverblue/Bluefin base image. Runs as root under systemd.

Read docs/ARCHITECTURE.md before changing the firewall or routing paths; several
rules here look redundant and are not (see the INVARIANT comments).
"""
